<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) != null || \old(this.get(i)) == null) && (this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i))) || \old(this.get(i)) == null);</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the index is valid, all elements before the specified index remain unchanged unless they were initially `null`. The condition `(this.get(i) != null || \old(this.get(i)) == null)` handles the case where the current element could be `null` but was not `null` previously, and vice versa. The main part of the assertion checks that the elements are equal if they were not `null` initially.
